  "reviewedFrom": "Bank reconciliation practice: statement opening + statement activity = statement closing; GL control balance = statement balance adjusted by outstanding book items (checks/deposits in transit); each bank line is owned by exactly one book entry; card purchases are expensed once when charged and a card repayment only moves cash to the card liability; transfers between accounts move cash without income or expense. Pending licensed-CPA review (B16.3). Amounts are integer cents.",
