      "derivation": "Cutover: bank 10,000, check 998 (1,200) outstanding, book 8,800. October: check 301 (1,000) written and voided; check 998 voided by journal. Before offsets the statement shows four outstanding entries netting to zero (the imported check among them). An offset whose entries do not cancel is refused; the two cancelling pairs clear. The statement then closes with nothing outstanding and both offsets recorded in its evidence: statement 9,985 = book 9,985. The voided check leaves the bill owed again (AP 1,000) and cash counts the 1,000 once: written and voided.",
